# Product & design

## Purpose

B2B website for Mandalon — chip packaging, wire bonding, and consulting.

- **Primary goal:** Generate contact inquiries from technical buyers
- **Secondary goals:** Educate, build trust, showcase expertise
- **Not:** e-commerce, consumer marketing, app-style UI

## Audience

- **Who:** CEO, R&D leads, CTO, project managers
- **What they need:** proof of expertise, practical capability info, easy contact, emergency help with wire bonding
- **Tone:** Professional, practical, experience-based, clarity over hype

## Design principles

- Prefer **clarity and trust** over visual flair
- **One visual treatment per pattern** — unify similar elements; avoid subtle one-off variants
- Use design tokens from `app.css` — see `styling.mdc` for CSS details

## Usability

- Pages must be **scannable** — clear headings, lead text, logical sections
- **Readable line length** — use `PageContent` (applies `.text-width`)
- **Contact path** must stay obvious from main pages
- **Mobile:** usable down to ~320px; test breakpoints around 780–900px
- **Languages:** Swedish default, English via `/en/…` — no hardcoded locale strings in pages

## Accessibility (baseline)

- One `<h1>` per page; logical heading order
- Meaningful `alt` on content images; `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons
- Iframes need a descriptive `title` (see contact map)
- Links readable without color alone; do not remove focus styles
- Be mindful with semantic elements to help screen readers work properly

## When designing new UI

- Reuse shared components before inventing page-specific layouts
- Demo new variants on the experiment page (`/(dev)/experiment`, available in `npm run dev` only) before using in production pages
